Design for Refill on the Go is a design strategy focused on enabling users to easily refill products while on the move, thereby promoting convenience and encouraging reuse. This strategy emphasizes the importance of designing products that can be refilled quickly and efficiently in various settings, such as on-the-go or in public spaces. By incorporating features like portable refill stations or refillable packaging formats, Design for Refill on the Go aims to minimize single-use packaging waste and promote a more sustainable consumption behavior among users. This strategy aligns with the principles of a maintenance circular business model by extending the lifespan of products through repeated refills, ultimately reducing the overall environmental impact associated with traditional single-use products. Research has shown that incorporating refillable options into product design can not only reduce packaging waste but also lead to cost savings for both businesses and consumers, making it a key strategy in advancing circular economy principles within the consumer goods industry.